## Full check (the gate that did not pass)

Command:
`HEAVY_PRIORITY=p2 HEAVY_RUN_TIMEOUT_S=1800 HEAVY_MIN_AVAIL_MB=1500 HEAVY_PREFLIGHT_WAIT_S=3600 bash /home/daniebo/Desktop/advantage-pr/scripts/jobs/heavy-run.sh -c 'pnpm architecture:check'`

- start = 2026-11-18T18:52:29+07:00
- end = 2026-11-18T18:53:24+07:00
- exit = 1 (the CLI exits 2; `pnpm` maps it to 1, and heavy-run reports 1)
- HEAD = `98c0a553a8f3d0b9454acf5175ddf15c8c4f51a0` at start and at end; unchanged
- output: `architecture check: analysis-error (files=7009, findings=884, parseErrors=1)`
- the one parse error: `MODULE_RESOLUTION_ERROR apps/accounting/next-env.d.ts:4:1`
- the debt comparison did not run, so this run holds no additions, removals, or renames count

Cause (read-only inspection):

- Three `next-env.d.ts` files carry uncommitted working-tree edits from a dev server:
  `apps/accounting/next-env.d.ts` (modified 2026-11-13 05:46), `apps/marketing/next-env.d.ts`
  (modified 2026-11-06 01:10), and `apps/activity-vinext-fixture/next-env.d.ts` (modified
  2026-11-06 01:12). The whole-worktree status holds these three modified files and no other
  modified file.
- The working-tree form of `apps/accounting/next-env.d.ts` adds
  `import "./.next/types/root-params.d.ts";` at line 4. `apps/accounting/.next/types/` does not
  exist in this checkout.
- `nextGeneratedRouteTypeTarget` (`packages/architecture-enforcement/src/analyzer.ts:415-426`)
  accepts only `next-env.d.ts` imports that match `^\./\.next\/(?:dev\/)?types\/routes\.d\.ts$`.
  A `root-params.d.ts` import therefore fails to resolve and becomes a parse error.
- `checkArchitectureRepository` (`architecture-check.ts:200-229`) reads working-tree bytes for
  the analysis. The refresh and the manifest validation read the projection, which takes HEAD
  bytes for every path outside `packages/architecture-enforcement`. That is why the refresh and
  its validate step passed and this check does not.

The working-tree edits are unrelated to this track. This role does not restore, stash, or commit
them. The gate needs one of two decisions: restore the three generated files, or accept a check
on HEAD bytes. Task 1.4 stays `[~]`.

